fix(F035.6): address codex P2s + green CI

- test_database: add consolidation_cycles/actions to the expected table set
  (CI runs against Postgres where migration 063 creates them; the assertion
  flagged them as Extra). Verified passing with NOUS_TEST_DB=postgres.
- codex P2 (stale_scan): buffer deactivated facts and emit audit rows only
  AFTER session.commit() succeeds — a rolled-back transaction must not leave
  the audit reporting deactivations that never landed.
- codex P2 (F031): same class of bug — record the contradiction action only
  when contradictions_resolved actually advanced (i.e. the apply committed),
  not before the apply try-block.
- codex P2 (ordering): add a monotonic per-cycle `seq` column; batched action
  inserts share created_at=now() so it can't order ties. Auditor stamps seq at
  record time; dashboard detail orders by seq ASC NULLS LAST, created_at.

Validated end-to-end on real Postgres (seq inserts 0..n, dashboard returns
actions in recording order). 114 prior tests still green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
